    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58915" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κοννᾶς</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κόννος</span></b> , ὁ, a famous harpist who
		taught Socrates, <i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>Euthd.</u>
			272c
		</span></i>, but died in want, <i><span class="en">
			Cratin.
			317
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Eq.</u>
			534
		</span></i>: hence prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κόννου θρῖον</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>trifle</i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				673
			</span></i>; altered to K. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψῆφος</span> by
			Ar.l.c.</div>
